[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mdeepseek_deepseek-v4-flash-failing-tests-trial-3[0m[0m
All 15 tests pass. Here's a summary of the 9 fixes across 3 files:

**`src/auth.py`** — 2 bugs
- `has_permission`: Made the `in` check case-insensitive by comparing `.lower()` on both sides
- `is_admin_or_owner`: Changed `and` to `or` — the function returns `True` when the user is an admin *or* matches the resource owner

**`src/inventory.py`** — 4 bugs
- `__init__`: Replaced mutable default `{}` with `None` + copy-on-assign so two `Inventory()` calls don't share the same dict
- `add`: Changed `self._stock[sku] = qty` to `self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty` so it accumulates instead of overwriting
- `reserve`: Changed `>=` to `>` so reserving exactly the available stock succeeds instead of raising `OutOfStock`
- `release`: Added a guard `if qty > current: raise ValueError(...)` so releasing more than reserved raises an error

**`src/text_utils.py`** — 3 bugs
- `slugify`: Added `char.lower()` on alphanumeric chars so the result is lowercase
- `slugify`: Replaced `.replace("--", "-")` with `re.sub(r"-+", "-")` so runs of 3+ dashes fully collapse (single-pass replace misses cascading)
- `truncate`: Changed `text[:max_len]` to `text[:max_len - len(suffix)]` so the output respects `max_len` including the suffix length
